 "_about": "File manifest of drydock_eval/contain/reference. `sha256` is the released file; `verified_source_sha256` is the file of the authors' deployment that the canaries and controls reported in the write-up were run with. A released file differs from it by the licence header, by host-specific constants (paths, account and host names, a port, labels of private agent bundles), and in two canary files by one rewritten check (GUIDE section 7); the authors keep a per-file diff. Because the header changes every hash, the released tree has its own runner, library and harness hashes: it has not been run in a container by the authors and no gate file exists for it.",
 "_verbatim": {
  "lib/seccomp_g4s_d41.json": "A Docker seccomp profile, shipped byte-identical because the library pins its sha256 and Docker reads the file: it carries no licence field. It is the default profile of the Moby project (github.com/moby/profiles, seccomp/default.json, v0.2.3, Apache-2.0) with the Linux AIO system calls removed and an explicit rule denying io_uring, as produced by tools/make_seccomp_d41.py; distributed here under Apache-2.0. The attribution and the statement of the change are in the NOTICE file at the top of the package."
 },
